# Frontend: clean, reusable, fast

## Layers (do not skip)

```
app/**/page.tsx  →  features/*/components  →  features/*/hooks  →  features/*/api
                 →  components/patterns | components/ui | lib/*
```

- Pages are thin: compose a feature component; no fetch or form logic in the route file.
- Hooks own React Query; `api/` owns HTTP. Components never call the proxy directly.
- Prefer server components; add `'use client'` only for interactivity or browser APIs.

## Clean

- One job per component. Split if it mixes list + form + dialog + unrelated fetch.
- Colocate feature UI under `features/<domain>/components/`; share only true cross-domain UI.
- Name by role: `StudentsList`, `useStudents`, `adminKeys.students()` — not `Helper`, `utils2`.
- Handle loading / empty / error explicitly (`QueryState`, empty CTA, mapped errors). No silent catch.

## Reusable

- Reach for `components/patterns/*` before inventing (DataTable, PageHeader, MoneyText, StatusBadge, PermissionGate, IconActionButton).
- **Row / table actions are icon-only** (`IconActionButton` / `IconActionLink`) with `aria-label` + `title` — never text like “View” / “Edit” / “Archive” in dense tables.
- `components/ui/*` = primitives only. Domain wording and school logic stay in features or patterns.
- Extract a hook when the same query/mutation appears twice; share query keys via `api/keys`.
- Forms: one schema (Zod), field errors from `mapError`, disable submit while pending, reuse idempotency key per intent.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — page fetches + renders everything
'use client';
export default function Page() { /* useQuery + 200 lines UI */ }

// ✅ GOOD — thin page, feature owns UI + hook
import { ClassesPage } from '@/features/admin/components/structure';
export default function Page() { return <ClassesPage />; }
```

## Speed

- Keep client JS lean: no heavy libs in parent/student home; lazy-load rare dialogs/charts.
- List state (page, sort, filters) in the URL; do not refetch on every keystroke — debounce search.
- Invalidate only the affected query keys after mutations; avoid blanket `invalidateQueries()`.
- Tables: virtualise large pages; images/files via signed URLs on demand (never cache signed URLs).
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion`. Prefer CSS over JS animation for simple transitions.

## Never

- Duplicate pattern components inside a feature.
- Float math for money — use minor units + `MoneyText` / `MoneyInput`.
- Check role names in UI — use `can('…')` / `PermissionGate`.
- Add stubs or fake API responses; call real OpenAPI operations only.
